%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: NonaIntroDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Good evening. You are new here. You are the fifth officer to work
      this post. Nona Beridze. Census recorder, district eleven. Eleven years.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: My job is to know who lives where and who has moved. In normal circumstances that is administrative. Right now it is something else.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: What do you mean, something else?
      npcResponse: "The gaps are larger now. Names that stop appearing. I cross-reference before I close a file. I always cross-reference."
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    - playerChoiceText: That sounds like difficult work.
      npcResponse: It requires attention. I am good at attention. Most people find sustained attention uncomfortable. I have never understood why.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
  - type: 0
    npcLine: I live alone. I prefer it. Shared spaces complicate the records. I
      have been through this checkpoint thirty-one times; I know your processing
      time to within four seconds. You have a good face for records — very consistent.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: I noted your face the moment you sat down. It is not personal. It
      is simply what I do. My documents. I filed them myself. Everything is accurate.
      I double-check.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: You noted my face?
      npcResponse: "I note everything. The last officer\u2019s face, too. And the ones before him. I find the continuity useful."
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    - playerChoiceText: That's a little unusual.
      npcResponse: "So I\u2019ve been told. Usually by people whose names I already had written down."
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
